data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":670,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_019b470727bced9e016ac947952d48819097fb788eeb8dcc48","call_id":"call_2c276be5dfb943aa8e42a5625707700e","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"<select id=\\\"task-filter\\\" name=\\\"filter\\\" onchange=\\\"this.form.requestSubmit()\\\">\",\"newText\":\"<select id=\\\"task-filter\\\" name=\\\"filter\\\" onchange=\\\"submitTaskFilter(this.form)\\\">\"},{\"oldText\":\" onchange=\\\"this.form.requestSubmit()\\\">\\n            <label for=\\\"task-${task.id}\\\">\",\"newText\":\" onchange=\\\"saveCompletion(this)\\\">\\n            <label for=\\\"task-${task.id}\\\">\"},{\"oldText\":\"    </section>`);\\n}\\n\\nfunction redirectToProject\",\"newText\":\"    </section>\\n    <p id=\\\"save-error\\\" role=\\\"alert\\\" hidden>Unable to save task completion. Please try again.</p>\\n    <script>\\n      const pendingTaskSaves = new Set();\\n\\n      function saveCompletion(input) {\\n        const completed = input.checked;\\n        const form = input.form;\\n        const body = new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form));\\n        input.disabled = true;\\n        document.getElementById('save-error').hidden = true;\\n        const save = (async () => {\\n          try {\\n            const response = await fetch(form.action, {\\n              method: 'POST', body, headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },\\n            });\\n            if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Save failed');\\n            const filter = body.get('filter');\\n            if ((filter === 'Open' && completed) || (filter === 'Completed' && !completed)) {\\n              form.closest('[data-testid=\\\"task-row\\\"]').remove();\\n            }\\n          } catch {\\n            input.checked = !completed;\\n            document.getElementById('save-error').hidden = false;\\n          } finally {\\n            input.disabled = false;\\n          }\\n        })();\\n        pendingTaskSaves.add(save);\\n        save.finally(() => pendingTaskSaves.delete(save));\\n        return save;\\n      }\\n\\n      async function submitTaskFilter(form) {\\n        await Promise.all([...pendingTaskSaves]);\\n        form.requestSubmit();\\n      }\\n    </script>`);\\n}\\n\\nfunction redirectToProject\"},{\"oldText\":\"      redirectToProject(response, project.id, filter);\",\"newText\":\"      if (taskId && request.headers.accept === 'application/json') {\\n        response.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });\\n        response.end(JSON.stringify({ status: 'ok' }));\\n      } else {\\n        redirectToProject(response, project.id, filter);\\n      }\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":671,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_019b470727bced9e016ac94789d3848190a6822d1510516804","object":"response","created_at":1791575945,"completed_at":1791575965,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_019b470727bced9e016ac9478b144c8190b0624efc808229b9","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Working through form handling**\n\nI’m focusing on a simple form that uses a promise to set up tracking of its state. I need to ensure that the `onchange` function calls `saveCompletion` reliably. I’m thinking about using `waitForTaskSaves(this.form)` to manage the flow. Additionally, I want to test the VM functions to assert that a fake fetch operation won’t omit any navigation payload, especially when there are unchecked and redirecting elements. That seems crucial."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqyUeVqEfoDHq-J-lcgsu0UIKasYHYnkfXOi3TCT3uRsTuE6AsN5V-CxzP9pqeLndN5Ov0NlWllo6moB8nwE_MPobT4Znl58iLP7s4pG0QyHPvf_II6JouMsFz4lPctjGyj1QihsqpsqfvY1WpE0pNcQhQ9jbRFfSQizejF2hbA02KFI3vvBNLDrISkYE6Fk-jMPM7Dg7FHlwnZWhy4wGSvyqz5aM2_-VyygvtA2_JWLAA7nJk9feZ84hw0iZWNo_TkDTdOsE7JHjY8cY60ZDN1KUEN8XWPA08KBcy3CuZp-LszX7zSAT5PPtGlebMVG6fIJmBKOxoU-da_SMmIzZvk59MfkLd-TsftRQgboYbymQsraUstlWQLM_NyxH0gJT-md4yOdufO67HsVFeu6tqnoaV3j0ISUX9DbaHJghq9wZdguNBhn0Ghz5Til9lagmYPju_WFx-PhSyn_damu7pTi-w469qFO24K2f_xyRfUCqgF-zjtKhphS9bsFPaIVk_hRnNq7Qgk81342NRhzi_vzjxBxwN8OkI9VX13X8LmiRVO6fOJy3-gr8yVxR3C_mTjuE4ADW72ELVuPBqevoeSnZNYpLpxdepMF37Px71lphO2QItAwkW9QxzyE-vf_JVm3SbCE8Xq8npIrH3XY6yzcbFcI1vBcSYKMqT5ukLVWlRVH9DAs7etJeJR4_JMOeJRN11wxgbw9o6PiBB3naytplSZqKgOF1xEzMlHc6bqQYkAFDyK7aLTZ1GOBhOkGLoW-Cl1MwTjLpK0-slShSrqV-Aw1iakzUo2HRhs2mTkvwa1iD-JDS253QNinAhG6U6qTHec6AaS1br_RUh599xUzsZPMb0sh-vOxcLvMuE7PSEk_LnYYxYrW-PiXy7ZZkh8DpvvgE5wDJj_LtAtRfOdKAG3P88Njy-CT00Ncz_ENj4NSQE3DkN-sJSLIy45ExLJkY1B3fBRKIOlCTeY7AigClK1zPaI-Jp74gxOqG9ohKEkwXAvJeFqYr_QnDr6IbtbYcyEGQkLXRuUC_9rZZ_vM2Kgpz_IDNfhDaMPVD6BGs401FfQlBEzTrwoF308jlODEIEzAzr2mhFpz6aolx2oAJWLhYBmrLPbq5jMNmvpnPLHSyA93rZQv6ej0A2o6LInQBPt0y9T7dW7OGlL7A8gqX6bqMmih_KXs2F1VQFiL4222FHKuM_mskjLXJF9WSt1a5Ay6RuC48QFYeRN06LCqiwKsgZFQR2wQbgX6E2t-O2RRLkmdVvIKd4uxyxe-NBYZSSKZqlZrFK2B65REnuQupADWeKroc0niqGEot1hQOqd_eSf1f2QSLYehC-LOMNeY_hE_Kvj0eZ0CaKjU1tVCc9Qsc-YWdx9wyeMu-gFQyDUVC8ixywEQtzGPYhqgPISn9rgg1MsXxDOwA1MUwycHKMMknTiIJMcc7MlcG1YWS6QfldFQmf1eu5ieOp-yV28a24LSaGXd5_1n_rVp5T2-M2lOJynhbreo3fUZqMJGuQxTzcbK5MLqUFqLUKRU1FnuEEU8nk_Um43ydv5yjt06laIqvrplfJpGNhPMbDS7w1_3vLLPzEhojwFL2rhCHPBiXuiR_bkXUBK6STMOKmMLDeAELXmPYv1qNkgn1w_dQ8mqvb2eM27bCkgQGbC6bSl1b6_iBCGW5hjUit60K9E9arB6ABvuz-x3l2uxQmOMHm6l7AJEXWABJQBO6qBEFLnqFgKWKScXn8hdtNmf3AztJ0ZHQYjln7exvNKvYBBg9TCpYKnF_qWdGwNXoBrDDmN8ggrpin9ghvJ0yLmZk9_QT3kaV_WNWxdJK7QAMG-frFlI62D02QEJauNPKzm8eGX11H4IxiLIlrdFHDqeNQbET_kKqGyPptTtVofvRoew61_PKxCSIfZKLlb5zd50sUhv6WD42S2WZjcRg